pngdeer's changes to libaom 3.15.2 (apply with patch -p1 in its source; FINDINGS.md round 7):

- No SIMD for aom_hadamard_16x16 and av1_quantize_fp. From speed 8 all-intra calls these 8-bit functions on 10-bit
  coefficients too; their C copes (32-bit sums, clamping) and their SIMD doesn't, so its bytes would differ from the C's.
  With them in C, libaom's SIMD (CONFIG_EXCLUDE_SIMD_MISMATCH=1) wrote plain C's bytes on every encode checked.
- PNGDEER_STILL=1 leaves the sub-pixel, compound, masked and OBMC functions, which only inter frames use, and the 8- and
  12-bit high bit depth sets out of the encoder's function tables, so a still-image build links less code. Without the
  define nothing changes.

--- a/aom_dsp/aom_dsp_rtcd_defs.pl
+++ b/aom_dsp/aom_dsp_rtcd_defs.pl
@@ -1284,7 +1284,7 @@
   specialize qw/aom_hadamard_8x8 sse2 neon/;
 
   add_proto qw/void aom_hadamard_16x16/, "const int16_t *src_diff, ptrdiff_t src_stride, tran_low_t *coeff";
-  specialize qw/aom_hadamard_16x16 avx2 sse2 neon/;
+  # pngdeer: no SIMD aom_hadamard_16x16; SSE2/AVX2 add 10-bit coefficients in 16 bits, the C in 32 (allintra speed 8+)
 
   add_proto qw/void aom_hadamard_32x32/, "const int16_t *src_diff, ptrdiff_t src_stride, tran_low_t *coeff";
   specialize qw/aom_hadamard_32x32 avx2 sse2 neon/;
